Package: EpiTracer
Title: Calling and Visualising Episomal Extrachromosomal DNA from WGS
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Alhafidz", "Hamdan", , "alhafidz.hamdan@ed.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for detecting episomal extrachromosomal
    DNA (ecDNA) amplicons (ecDNAs formed by simple DNA excision events, instead of complex dsDNA breaks i.e. chromothripsis) from whole-genome sequencing data and for visualising
    the structural rearrangements underlying focal amplifications. The episomal
    ecDNA caller identifies duplication breakpoints at amplicon boundaries,
    checks for excision scars, and classifies amplicons as episomal in origin.
    The rearrangement plotter draws linear allele-specific copy-number and
    structural-variant "recon" plots across one or more loci.
